# Line endings.
#
# Every line in a text file ends with an invisible marker. Windows writes one
# kind, macOS and Linux write another. Without this file git treats that marker
# as content, so a Windows editor that rewrites a file can turn a 46-line change
# into a 29,000-line diff: every line looks changed because every line now ends
# differently. That happened on 2026-09-06 and made the change under it
# unreviewable.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git: work out for yourself which files are text, and
# always store them with the Linux marker. Editors on Windows read that
# perfectly well, so nothing changes for anyone working there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched. Rewriting a marker inside a PNG corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
